WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.960
With nine films spread out over nearly two&nbsp;
decades, and a release order that jumps all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:10.240
around the chronological timeline, it's fair if&nbsp;
Fast &amp; Furious fans need a bit of a refresher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.920
on where we wound up after each one. Here's the&nbsp;
ending of every Fast and Furious film, explained.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:21.680
Despite functioning for most of its runtime as&nbsp;
practically a beat-for-beat "Point Break" remake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:26.560
"The Fast and the Furious" notably diverges&nbsp;
from the iconic surfer thriller in its ending.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:32.640
While the 1991 film sees protagonist Johnny&nbsp;
Utah release sympathetic antagonist Bodhi only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.440
to certain death, "The Fast and the Furious"&nbsp;
has its law enforcement hero, Brian O'Conner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.560
let his law-skirting frenemy go free. He&nbsp;
even gives him an assist on his way out.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:48.080
After initially getting close to Dominic Toretto&nbsp;
only as a means to ferret out the details of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:53.200
high-speed heist operation, Brian eventually&nbsp;
comes to realize that he genuinely cares about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:58.640
Dom and his crew. Dom and his sister Mia feel&nbsp;
betrayed when they learn Brian's true identity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:01.280
and subsequently attempt to cut ties with him.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.600
However, Brian chases Dom down in a&nbsp;
winner-takes-all quarter-mile race,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.960
with the implied stakes being that, if he wins,&nbsp;
Dom will cooperate with being arrested. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.880
even though Dom crashes his car and Brian wins&nbsp;
the race, Brian opts to give Dom his own car,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:22.640
allowing him to escape instead of arresting him.&nbsp;
The film ends with Dom driving free in Mexico,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:26.800
and Brian having chosen their friendship&nbsp;
over his career as a police officer.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.400
Following his decision to facilitate Dom's&nbsp;
escape at the end of "The Fast and the Furious,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.120
Brian goes on the run, making a living&nbsp;
competing in underground street races.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:42.080
Eventually, Brian is arrested, but cuts a&nbsp;
deal with the FBI to go undercover and help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:47.120
bring down a drug lord in exchange for a clean&nbsp;
criminal record. To assist him, Brian recruits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:52.400
his estranged childhood friend Roman Pearce,&nbsp;
who is on parole and could use a similar deal.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:57.760
Brian and Roman take down the drug lord with&nbsp;
the help of U.S. Customs agent Monica Fuentes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:02.800
leading to his arrest and full pardons for&nbsp;
the two ex-convicts. Unbeknownst to the FBI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:06.800
though, Roman sets aside some of the&nbsp;
drug lord's laundered money for himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:11.520
although he does turn over the rest. Free once&nbsp;
more, Brian suggests the two of them use the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:15.840
money to open a garage together in Miami...&nbsp;
although that doesn't wind up happening.

00:02:16.871 --> 00:02:20.720
The only main Fast and Furious film&nbsp;
not to center around Dom or Brian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:26.000
"Tokyo Drift" follows teenager Sean Boswell,&nbsp;
who is sent to Tokyo to live with his dad after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.520
destroying most of a residential construction&nbsp;
site in a drag race in Arizona. Relocating to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:36.800
different continent doesn't do much to curb Sean's&nbsp;
speedster ways, and he quickly falls in love with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:41.920
the Japanese street racing scene. The Japanese&nbsp;
drivers all employ the technique of drifting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:46.560
which allows cars to maneuver around&nbsp;
curves and corners using controlled skids.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.960
After initially failing at drifting, Sean&nbsp;
eventually masters the skill with the help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:56.640
of a local racer named Han. Unfortunately, not&nbsp;
long after Han has taken Sean under his wing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.680
the Yakuza come after Han for stealing from&nbsp;
them. A high-speed chase ensues, and it appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:06.720
that Han is killed. The final act of "Tokyo&nbsp;
Drift" sees Sean challenging a Yakuza member's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:12.080
nephew to a race, which will determine which&nbsp;
of them is allowed to remain safely in Tokyo.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:17.840
Using his newfound drifting skills, Sean wins.&nbsp;
Now established as the Drift King of Tokyo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.840
Sean continues racing, and the film&nbsp;
closes with an American arriving to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:26.320
challenge him to a race — Dominic Toretto,&nbsp;
who claims that he used to work with Han.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:32.480
Along with the next two films, the fourth film in&nbsp;
the franchise actually takes place between "2 Fast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:38.160
2 Furious" and "Tokyo Drift." After "Tokyo Drift"&nbsp;
ended with the reveal that Dom and Han used to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:43.680
work together, "Fast &amp; Furious" cuts back to that&nbsp;
time, five years after the end of the first film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:48.480
The film opens with Dom stealing fuel tankers&nbsp;
in the Dominican Republic with a crew that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:53.040
includes Han as well as Dom's girlfriend,&nbsp;
Letty. Meanwhile, after getting his criminal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:59.040
record expunged at the end of "2 Fast 2 Furious,"&nbsp;
Brian O'Conner is now working as an FBI agent.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:03.680
Dom and Brian's paths eventually cross when&nbsp;
Dom hears that Letty has been killed, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:09.040
search for her killer leads him to a Mexican drug&nbsp;
lord that Brian is also attempting to track down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:14.400
Together, the two team up to apprehend the drug&nbsp;
lord, and Brian manages to arrest him, with Dom's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:19.600
help. In the process, Dom kills one of the drug&nbsp;
lord's henchmen whom he blames for Letty's death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:25.600
making Brian's attempts to clear his name futile.&nbsp;
The film ends with Dom being sentenced to 25 years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:31.920
to life in prison. Unable to accept this outcome,&nbsp;
Brian resigns from the FBI and teams up with Mia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:35.360
along with a couple members of Dom's&nbsp;
crew, to break him out of prison.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.200
The film ends with Brian leading a group&nbsp;
of cars to intercept Dom's prison bus.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:44.640
Picking up directly on the heels of "Fast&nbsp;
&amp; Furious," "Fast Five" opens with Brian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:49.040
and his accomplices breaking Dom out of&nbsp;
prison. Together with Mia, they flee to Rio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:53.760
de Janeiro. By this time, Brian and Mia have&nbsp;
rekindled their romance from the first film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:57.520
and during the course of the film,&nbsp;
Mia makes a game-changing revelation.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:04:58.800
"We have no choice but to split up."

00:04:58.800 --> 00:04:59.300
"I'm pregnant."

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.800
In order to build a new life, Dom and Brian&nbsp;
hatch a scheme to steal $100 million from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:09.360
a major crime lord, which requires them to&nbsp;
recruit a crew to help pull off the heist.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:14.240
This includes Han from "Tokyo Drift"&nbsp;
and Roman from "2 Fast 2 Furious,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:20.560
along with Tej, Gisele, Leo, and Santos.&nbsp;
Meanwhile, Diplomatic Security Service Agent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:26.160
Luke Hobbs and local Brazilian police officer&nbsp;
Elena Neves are in pursuit of Brian and Dom.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:31.280
However, after the crime lord's men murder&nbsp;
Hobbs' team, he and Elena agree to join forces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:36.240
with Brian and Dom to help with the heist. In a&nbsp;
spectacularly destructive series of events that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:41.040
involves dragging a safe through the city behind&nbsp;
fast-moving cars, the group is successful in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:46.480
stealing the money. After killing the crime lord,&nbsp;
Hobbs agrees to give Brian and Dom a 24-hour head&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:51.920
start, provided they leave the money. The duo&nbsp;
agree, but only because they've already secretly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:57.120
swapped out the money. The real loot is divided&nbsp;
amongst the crew, who scatter across the globe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:01.840
each with a hefty pile of cash. At the end of&nbsp;
the film, Dom and Elena, who are now a couple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:07.120
relax on a beach with Brian and Mia. Meanwhile,&nbsp;
unbeknownst to them, Monica Fuentes from "2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:11.680
Fast 2 Furious" gives Hobbs a file that&nbsp;
shows that Letty is actually still alive.

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:17.680
Living large following their successful heist at&nbsp;
the end of "Fast Five," Dom's crew is eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:22.880
reunited by Luke Hobbs, who reaches out to&nbsp;
Dom for assistance in capturing a terrorist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:28.080
named Owen Shaw. Working as a member of Shaw's&nbsp;
crew is Letty, who has completely lost her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:33.680
memories of her life before she disappeared in the&nbsp;
fourth movie. Motivated by a desire to find Letty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:39.680
and restore her memories, Dom's crew teams up to&nbsp;
track down Shaw, although he eventually gets away.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:44.800
In the process, Dom saves Letty's life, prompting&nbsp;
her to decide to switch sides and stay with him.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:50.720
The final act of the film sees Dom's crew pursuing&nbsp;
Shaw to a runway, where Dom's group is determined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:54.960
to keep Shaw's plane from taking off with&nbsp;
its weapons of mass destruction. They're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.960 --> 00:07:00.560
successful in stopping Shaw, but Gisele is killed&nbsp;
in the process of saving Han. Shaw is grievously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:05.360
injured after being thrown from the plane and&nbsp;
is subsequently arrested by Hobbs, who secures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:10.320
pardons for Dom and his crew as payment for their&nbsp;
assistance. At the end of the film, although Letty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:15.840
still doesn't have her memories, Elena graciously&nbsp;
steps aside to allow her and Dom to be together.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:19.840
Meanwhile, a grieving Han decides to&nbsp;
take his Fast Five money to Tokyo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:23.680
where he and Gisele had once talked about&nbsp;
moving, which is what puts him there at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:27.920
beginning of "Tokyo Drift." In a mid-credits&nbsp;
scene, it is revealed that the person whose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:32.400
car crashed into Han in that film was&nbsp;
driven by Owen Shaw's brother, Deckard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:36.480
who is now seeking vengeance on the people&nbsp;
who injured and captured his brother.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:41.600
The seventh "Fast and the Furious" film&nbsp;
picks up just before the sixth film ends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:46.320
showing Deckard Shaw stealing information on&nbsp;
Dom's crew from Hobbs' office, injuring Hobbs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:51.920
in the process. Shortly after that, Shaw attacks&nbsp;
Han in Tokyo, which we previously saw both in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:57.440
middle of "Tokyo Drift" and at the end of "Fast&nbsp;
&amp; Furious 6." As Shaw targets the rest of Dom's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:03.440
crew, a mysterious government operative named Mr.&nbsp;
Nobody offers to help Dom stop Shaw if Dom's team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:08.960
can assist him. Mr. Nobody needs help recovering&nbsp;
a computer tracking program, called God's Eye,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:14.000
as well as its creator, a hacker named&nbsp;
Ramsey, who has been kidnapped by terrorists.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:19.840
After rescuing Ramsey, Dom's team manages to help&nbsp;
Mr. Nobody stop the terrorists and subdue Shaw,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:25.120
who is taken into custody by Hobbs. In the&nbsp;
process, Letty finally regains her memories,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:29.920
revealing that she and Dom actually got married&nbsp;
before they parted ways in the fourth film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:35.040
Meanwhile, Mia has announced that she's pregnant&nbsp;
again, and Brian decides that it's finally time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:40.080
for him to walk away from his dangerous life in&nbsp;
order to be with his family. The film ends with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:44.960
the crew bidding a fond farewell to Brian&nbsp;
as he drives off into the sunset, and Dom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:49.280
thinking back on all the happy memories they've&nbsp;
shared together. This ending also served as an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:54.560
emotional eulogy for Paul Walker, who died in an&nbsp;
unrelated accident during the film's production.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:59.840
After regaining her memories of their wedding,&nbsp;
the eighth Fast and the Furious film opens with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:05.040
Dom and Letty taking their long-overdue honeymoon&nbsp;
in Havana. Unfortunately, while they're there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:09.920
Dom is confronted by a cyberterrorist named&nbsp;
Cipher, who blackmails him into betraying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:14.400
his crew and helping her steal weapons. The&nbsp;
rest of Dom's crew — along with Hobbs and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:19.360
surprisingly, Deckard Shaw — are recruited&nbsp;
by Mr. Nobody to help them stop Cipher.

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:23.440
Eventually, it's revealed that Cipher&nbsp;
has captured Elena and her infant son;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:28.400
it turns out that Elena was pregnant when she and&nbsp;
Dom split up, and she never told him. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:33.600
while outwardly cooperating with Cipher, Dom&nbsp;
quietly tries to undermine her, which leads to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:38.720
Cipher having Elena executed. Ultimately, though,&nbsp;
Dom is able to get the upper hand by helping the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:43.840
Shaw brothers' mother, who repays the favor&nbsp;
by tasking her sons with rescuing Dom's son.

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:48.160
Once the Shaws have recovered the baby,&nbsp;
Dom turns on Cipher, thwarting her plans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:53.520
to incite nuclear war and reassuring his team&nbsp;
that he'd never really turned on them after all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:57.680
Unfortunately, though, Cipher manages&nbsp;
to escape before she can be apprehended.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:00.560
At the end of the film, Dom finally names his son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:05.680
while Hobbs decides to walk away from his job&nbsp;
with the Diplomatic Security Service for good.

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:09.040
"Everyone, meet Brian."

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:14.720
Following the events of "The Fate of the&nbsp;
Furious," Deckard Shaw learns that his sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:18.160
Hattie, has disappeared along&nbsp;
with a programmable supervirus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:23.280
and is tasked by the CIA to team up with Hobbs&nbsp;
in order to find her. Once they locate Hattie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:28.080
who is an MI6 agent, they learn that she only&nbsp;
infected herself with the virus in order to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:32.800
keep it from falling into the hands of Brixton&nbsp;
Lore, a terrorist who has been cybernetically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:38.320
augmented with superstrength. Brixton frames both&nbsp;
Shaw siblings, along with Hobbs, as terrorists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:42.880
and the trio flees to Hobbs' childhood home&nbsp;
in Samoa to figure out their next steps.

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:46.480
There, they prepare to make their&nbsp;
stand against Brixton's organization,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:51.200
Eteon, alongside Hobbs' brothers. As they&nbsp;
work to defeat Brixton and his soldiers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:54.880
one of Hobbs' brothers figures out&nbsp;
how to extract the virus from Hattie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.880 --> 00:11:00.080
even if the process is frustratingly slow. After&nbsp;
his defeat, Brixton is killed remotely by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:04.880
unseen director of Eteon, who then insinuates&nbsp;
that they'll be coming after Hobbs and Shaw.

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:12.800
"You don't remember me, do you Hobbs? You&nbsp;
will. It's gonna be a hell of a reunion."

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:17.360
However, Hobbs and Shaw are&nbsp;
unintimidated by Eteon's threats.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:20.880
The film ends with the Shaw siblings&nbsp;
breaking their mother out of prison&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:25.920
and Hobbs learning about the existence of another,&nbsp;
potentially even more dangerous supervirus.

